// Periods, calendar arithmetic, and the year-month and month-day types against reference data.
//
// The rows come from V8's built-in ECMAScript Temporal (`node --harmony-temporal`), except the
// `h` rows, which are hand-written. The V8 of Node 22 has the rules of an older draft in five
// places, and there the rows have the answer of the current specification:
// - A period outside the limits of the specification is rejected.
// - The `u` rows compare the day of the first date as written, so January 31 to February 28 is
//   28 days and not one month.
// - The `U` rows move the end date, not the start date, when the time of day goes against the
//   dates.
// - An annotation can follow the short forms `YYYY-MM` and `MM-DD`.
// - February 29 in a year without one is February 28 in the `D` rows.
//
// Each row is tab-separated, and its last field is the text that `Display` writes for the answer,
// or `!` when there is none:
// - `p`: a period text.
// - `a`: a date, a period, and the overflow rule (`c` constrain, `r` reject): the date reached.
// - `u`: two dates and the largest unit (`y`, `m`, `w`, `d`): the period from the first to the
//   second.
// - `A` and `U`: the same for a date and time.
// - `y`: a year and month text. `Y`: a year and month and a count of months to add. `n`: two
//   months and the count of months between them.
// - `d`: a month and day text. `D`: a month and day and a year: the date, with February 29 held
//   to the 28th.
// - `h`: a kind (`p`, `y`, `d`, or `D`), its input, and the `Debug` text of the answer, for the
//   reasons and offsets of rejected texts and for `Overflow.Reject`.

